# The DualSense trigger states of src/pc_triggers.cpp in one drive in free roam (development; run with
# --mcla_adaptive_triggers=true --mcla_trigger_log=true --mcla_trigger_release_unfocused=false, and
# --mcla_trigger_fake_device=true when no DualSense is connected). The checks read the log's "pc triggers:" lines
# between the marks (C:\mcv\pctrig\chain\run_triggers.py). Segments:
#   title, map_zoom, free_roam   as boot-to-roam.pad: no effect may be sent before the car is driven
#   trig_idle       standing at the spawn point: the throttle spring on R2 and the brake resistance on L2
#   trig_throttle1  full throttle out of the car park (as drive-spawn.pad) and straight on: gear changes, the shift speeds are learnt
#   trig_brake      full brake to a stop
#   trig_throttle2  full throttle again from a standstill: R2 buzzes near the top of the first gear
#   trig_nitro      X held (the nitro): R2 buzzes while it burns
#   trig_pause      Start with the car moving: both triggers slack; Start again: back
#   trig_option     mcla_adaptive_triggers off and on
#   trig_focus      the window minimised with mcla_trigger_release_unfocused on, then restored
#   trig_end        the end of the script: the game quits (mcla_pad_exit_on_end) and releases the triggers
include boot-to-roam.pad
log TRIG idle: standing at the spawn point
mark trig_idle
wait 3s 120f
log TRIG throttle1: full throttle out of the car park, straight on
mark trig_throttle1
trigger rt 1 50f
trigger rt 0.6
stick lx 1 40f
trigger rt 1
wait 12s 600f
log TRIG brake: full brake to a stop
mark trig_brake
trigger rt 0
trigger lt 1
wait 7s 300f
trigger lt 0
wait 2s 60f
log TRIG throttle2: full throttle from a standstill
mark trig_throttle2
trigger rt 1
wait 5s 240f
log TRIG nitro: X held with the throttle floored
mark trig_nitro
down x
wait 4s 180f
up x
wait 2s 60f
log TRIG pause: Start with the car moving
mark trig_pause
press start 4f
wait 3s 150f
log TRIG pause: Start again
press start 4f
wait 3s 150f
log TRIG option: off
mark trig_option
set mcla_adaptive_triggers false
wait 2s 60f
log TRIG option: on
set mcla_adaptive_triggers true
wait 2s 60f
log TRIG focus: window minimised
mark trig_focus
set mcla_trigger_release_unfocused true
window minimize
wait 3s
log TRIG focus: window restored
window restore
wait 3s
set mcla_trigger_release_unfocused false
wait 2s
release all
log TRIG end
mark trig_end
